# CODEOWNERS — auto-requests maintainer review on sensitive paths.
# Last matching pattern wins. MAINTAINERS.md and GOVERNANCE.md describe upstream's team and ladder;
# see FORK.md for how this fork is run.
#
# Scope principle: gate what CI can't catch (a bad change here passes the
# tests silently) + the catastrophic updater + governance docs. Code that
# test-all.mjs / Renovate / dependency-review already guard (scan.mjs,
# generate-pdf.mjs, test-all.mjs, package.json) is intentionally NOT gated,
# so routine contributor PRs aren't bottlenecked on a single owner.
#
# 2026-08-13: that condition is met — there is now more than one code owner,
# so the list broadens for the first time. The split is deliberate: the blocks
# below stay single-owner because they are the ones CI cannot catch and where
# a quiet mistake is expensive; the areas at the bottom move to the person who
# has been their de facto expert for months. Area ownership routes review;
# nothing enforces it on this fork (no branch protection beyond the
# protect-main ruleset, which only blocks deletion and force-push).

# Repo docs & governance
/README*.md            @jrmatherly
/CONTRIBUTING.md       @jrmatherly
/GOVERNANCE.md         @jrmatherly
/MAINTAINERS.md        @jrmatherly
/ARCHITECTURE.md       @jrmatherly
/.github/CODEOWNERS    @jrmatherly

# Coding-agent configuration (instructions, agent profiles, setup job):
# a change here rewrites what an autonomous session is allowed to do.
/.github/copilot-instructions.md  @jrmatherly
/.github/agents/                  @jrmatherly

# Agent behavior & the multi-CLI contract (prompt layer — CI-blind)
/CLAUDE.md             @jrmatherly
/AGENTS.md             @jrmatherly
/CODEX.md              @jrmatherly
/OPENCODE.md           @jrmatherly
/GEMINI.md             @jrmatherly
/KIMI.md               @jrmatherly
# The skill router. Every CLI's skill entrypoint (.claude/, .cursor/,
# .opencode/, .qwen/, .kimi/, .grok/, .antigravitycli/) is a symlink to this
# one file, so an edit here changes only this path — the symlinks never show
# up in the diff.
/.agents/skills/career-ops/SKILL.md  @jrmatherly

# Scoring & the system/user data contract (CI-blind; silent-danger)
/modes/_shared.md      @jrmatherly
/DATA_CONTRACT.md      @jrmatherly

# The self-updater (catastrophic if wrong — touches user installs)
/update-system.mjs     @jrmatherly
# Its system-layer list (#5554). Kept here: the run-time checks refuse an entry
# that names the user layer, not one that ships a file installs should not get.
/lib/update-manifest.mjs  @jrmatherly
/updater-migration-tests.mjs  @jrmatherly

# Plugin governance chokepoint (a bad change here ships unreviewed code to
# every user — the registry pin, the gates, and the CI must stay single-owner).
# The registry is one file per plugin under plugins-registry/ (#1401).
/plugins-registry/             @jrmatherly
/validate-plugin-registry.mjs  @jrmatherly
/plugin-install.mjs            @jrmatherly
/plugin-audit.mjs              @jrmatherly
/plugins/_engine.mjs           @jrmatherly
/plugins/_lock.mjs             @jrmatherly
/plugins/_net.mjs              @jrmatherly
/plugins/_registry.mjs         @jrmatherly
/.github/workflows/            @jrmatherly
/docs/PLUGIN_REVIEW.md         @jrmatherly

# The experimental web UI — owned by the web track (dual-track review with the
# core maintainer on any PR that also touches root files).
/web/ @jrmatherly

# ── Area owners ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not red lines: these are the day-to-day areas. On this fork every area
# routes to the fork owner; the code in them is upstream's, written by
# upstream's contributors. `test-all.mjs` itself stays out on purpose: it is
# the harness every other check runs through.
/tests/     @jrmatherly
/dashboard/ @jrmatherly
# Scanner providers and their contract suites are one reviewable unit: the
# module and its test land together, and the review that matters on a fetch
# surface is host allowlisting, redirects, SSRF, and parsing pinned with
# concrete assertions.
/providers/       @jrmatherly
/tests/providers/ @jrmatherly
